// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`renderMadr > renders a full accepted record 1`] = `
"# Add an @override decorator to typing

* Status: accepted
* Decided: 2023-02-14
* Source: Override decorator for static typing (PEP 698)
* Recovered by: DejaView (qwen3.5:9b)

## Context and Problem Statement

Type checkers flag a method marked @override when no base class defines it, catching overrides broken by a rename.

## Decision Outcome

Accepted: Add an @override decorator to typing.

### Reasons

* Renaming a base class method silently breaks subclasses today; the decorator makes that an error.
  * "a method meant to override a base class method no longer does once the base method is renamed" (lukas_w, 2022-11-08, verified) https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-698-override-decorator-for-static-typing/20839/1
* It costs nothing at runtime beyond setting one attribute.
  * "the only runtime effect is setting __override__ = True on the function" (lukas_w, 2022-12-13, verified) https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-698-override-decorator-for-static-typing/20839/22

## Links

* Code: \`Lib/typing.py\` (override), linked by pr_ref
* Code: \`Lib/test/test_typing.py\` (OverrideDecoratorTests), linked by pr_ref
* DejaView: https://dejaview.example/decisions/1
"
`;
